// An expression statement may be a bare TUPLE - `1, 2, 3` on a line of its own is legal
// Python (and test_grammar checks exactly that), so this takes an expression LIST. Assign
// is tried before it, so `a = 1` is unaffected.
ExprSmall   <~~ push(pyExprStmt(pop(), up.start, up.pos)) ~~>
            = ExprList ;

// Every expression production pushes exactly one thunk: function() -> value.
// A lambda binds loosest; then the a-if-c-else-b conditional expression; then
// the boolean/arith layers.
Expression  = Lambda | YieldExpr | Walrus | Ternary ;
// yield / yield from as an EXPRESSION (v = yield x): see makeYield.
YieldExpr   <~~ push(makeYield(takeAll(), up.pos)) ~~>
