// `a[0, 1:2]`, `m[:, ::2]`. CPython hands __getitem__ / __setitem__ a TUPLE whose
// sliced entries are slice objects (test_compile line 407 writes `d[1:2, 1:2] = 1`).
// Tried BEFORE SliceSfx and IndexSfx and gated on TupSliceAhead, so it fires only for
// the shape those two cannot parse. The value model has no slice type, so a sliced
// entry is the three-element tuple (start, stop, step) with None for an omitted bound,
// which keeps the key hashable as CPython's slice objects are.
SubTupSfx   <~~ push({kind: "index", idx: makeSubTuple(takeAll())}) ~~>
