// `for` statement takes: a name, a tuple of names, a nested or starred tuple
// (`for (kind, string, *_) in ...`) and even a subscript (`for tgt[0] in source()` - odd,
// but legal Python, and CPython's own suite tests both). compTargetOf keeps the
// all-plain-names case on its faster path, which is what keeps a comprehension
// variable LOCAL to the comprehension.
CompTarget  <~~ push(compTargetOf(takeAll())) ~~>
